    "done_when": "reckon/cli.py gains crew ack with required --run, --reason and --until options. The acknowledgement is stored through reckon/crew/runs.py beside record_run_disposition. reckon/crew/obligations.py leaves an acknowledged obligation out of the unacknowledged list while --until is in the future, returns it once --until has passed, and exposes the acknowledged items with their reason and until in a separate block that the hook and crew(view=obligations) can read. A new tests/test_crew_ack.py asserts: an acknowledged obligation leaves the list; it returns when its --until passes, derived from a fixture clock, not a literal date; the reason is read back; a malformed --until is refused; and the store writes only under a temporary config home. The declared mutation, ignoring the until time, fails the return case with its log recorded. tests/test_crew_obligations.py, tests/test_coordinator_obligations_hook.py, tests/test_mcp_crew_obligations.py, tests/test_obligations_do_not_mislead.py and the new file show zero added failures by id against the dispatch base, run with the absolute venv python and a neutral basetemp on node-local /tmp. baseline_suite and after_suite are one-line JSON with revision, tree, full command, exit_status, absolute log_path, completed, failure_count and failure_ids, negative_control_log is a top-level absolute path, and a tests: field is recorded. In reckon/cli.py only the new command is added",
